removed:
`maxLength` of a body field is measured by the written text of the field (a string — as is, another value — canonical JSON) at
any type of the value — as at the door (P/06.4 N2 `too_long`, the rule of the table [`requests-body`](../../06-console/vectors/requests-body/README.md));
the other words of the schema — over the JSON value.

The worker reads and files request rows and writes marks by operations of the store
[P/01.1](../../01-store/spec/01.1-store.norms.md) (a mark is a row-object, [P/05 N1.1](../../05-resource/spec/05-resource.norms.md));
it appends event lines to the files of its own server (the object store client contract «Operations» `ops`, `append`).

In the append profile
(`requests.outcome: fetched`) a body with an `action` from `elsewhere` is also an append: the holder checks the data and reports fetched;
`elsewhere` takes a row out of the mark procedure and out of the reaper only in the ordinary profile.

**Step 10.1.** The outcome is `{outcome: performed | refused, action?, reply?, ended_at}`; `reply` is the answer of perform, the same as in the event below ([request contract](../../common/contracts/request-mark.md) «Mark»); `action` is the value of the field `action` of the request body, not the handler name; a body
without `action` has no such field ([request contract](../../common/contracts/request-mark.md) «Mark»);
`error` MUST be present at `refused` and is absent at `performed`; if the outcome came after `unknown` (of the reaper or of another holder) — `late: true`.
